<urn:anqr:localisation-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Claiming a locale asserts that its key set is complete and its direction and script are handled. It does not assert that a native speaker has reviewed the translation, which is what communitytranslationcontribution exists to obtain." <urn:anqr:graph:localisation-model> .
<urn:anqr:localisation-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Observed at the legacy source: the interface template and every locale carried 1676 keys while en-US carried 1994, so 318 keys existed in exactly one locale. The legacy parity guard tolerated this by treating missing keys as normal. This model makes parity a blocking obligation instead, which is the substantive change rather than the locale count." <urn:anqr:graph:localisation-model> .
<urn:anqr:localisation-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Static content was observed at 105 locale directories against 87 interface locale files, so the two coverage sets were not the same. Parity is therefore declared separately for interface strings and for static content." <urn:anqr:graph:localisation-model> .
<urn:anqr:localisation-model:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "ANQR's complete language denominator: 86 claimed locales, 7 of them right-to-left, with the parity and direction obligations that make \"complete i18n\" checkable rather than aspirational." <urn:anqr:graph:localisation-model> .
